WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.330
Meiji 26 (1893)

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:54.610
My body... so heavy...

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.520
Just like this, I die.

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:05.060
Now, finally...

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:08.160
I can rest.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:15.100
After so many years have lapsed

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:26.340
Kaoru!

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:29.970
Tsubame...

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:33.410
Are you going to the harbor again?

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:39.590
Don't worry. I know he'll be back.

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:41.290
As you know,

00:02:41.290 --> 00:02:43.260
he comes back every time
no matter what happens.

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:02.640
Tsubame?

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:05.310
I just met Kaoru just outside the shop.

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:06.110
I see...

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:08.080
I can't stop myself from worrying about her.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:11.680
Kenji left and Kaoru is alone...

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:13.580
I'll go by her house later.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:15.050
Yahiko...

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:17.830
Do you think Kenshin was...

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:18.830
Hey!

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:21.800
But the war is over

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:24.490
and everybody is coming back
from the continent.

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:30.530
Even so, I know Kaoru is going
to the harbor every day.

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:33.410
She is always waiting

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:38.500
for Kenshin to come home.

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:57.130
The sun is sinking.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:59.800
I'm going to start preparing dinner.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:04.130
Haven't you changed your mind
about going back to Tokyo?

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:07.430
How about him?

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:09.380
What?

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:12.250
He hasn't come back yet?

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:14.080
Even if he comes back home,

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:16.240
I know that he'll go off somewhere soon.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.490
I've wondered since I was a kid,

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:24.050
why my mother married my father.

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:27.930
Then why did you come here?

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:30.870
It's useless for you to learn your
father's swordsmanship, isn't it?

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:35.270
I wanted to know what human strength was,

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:39.130
what true strength was!

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:58.080
Himura.

00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:00.600
Its been fifteen years since I saw you last time,

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:03.430
and I've come to see you to ask for a favor.

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:05.670
Please go to the continent.

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:12.800
I guess you already know that there
are some disputes on the continent.

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:15.540
I'm pretty sure that a war will be starting soon.

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:18.710
We have military force,

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:20.880
however, few soldiers of our understand battle.

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:25.250
If a person like you, who has
gone through many battles,

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:27.090
could be their leader...

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:31.430
Mr. Yamagata, I'd rather save people
who were hurt in the war

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:34.120
than put myself into one.

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:38.400
If war can't be avoided, the more I feel so.

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:40.170
Himura...

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:43.100
I will go to the continent to do just that.

00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:47.910
That's the only thing I can do now, and probably

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:50.140
the last thing I can do as my atonement.

00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:29.480
It's getting colder.

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:47.230
I will wait for you,
as I usually do, at this place

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:50.330
Until you return to me.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:55.980
So...

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:01.780
Good luck.

00:07:49.430 --> 00:07:50.760
Hey, Kaoru!

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:52.690
What's the matter?

00:07:56.140 --> 00:07:58.160
Answer me! Kaoru!

00:07:58.670 --> 00:07:59.710
Hey Kaoru!

00:07:59.710 --> 00:08:00.910
Recalling our past,

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:06.710
both you and I have lived with
scars that won't fade.

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:10.750
Scars which were carved as a cross...

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:22.900
I've cornered him. I won't let him
escape tonight. Hitokiri Battosai!

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:36.410
Is he the assassin who says he
belongs to my school of swordsmanship?

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:53.030
Help me clean the drill hall.

00:08:53.030 --> 00:08:55.900
Since you're staying at our house, you
can do things like that, can't you?

00:09:06.970 --> 00:09:08.080
Miss Kaoru.

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:09.040
What?

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:11.510
Kamiya Kasshin swordsmanship,

00:09:11.510 --> 00:09:14.480
created by your late father,
spares lives...

00:09:14.980 --> 00:09:18.480
The more I think about it, the more
I am impressed by his great will.

00:09:20.020 --> 00:09:21.250
You too, Kenshin.

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:23.490
Since you have great skill,

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:25.890
you could start a new school of swordsmanship
using your own methods.

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:30.930
What kind of swordsmanship do you
expect from my murdering sword?

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:39.170
I guess your father must have been
a gentle person, then?

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:44.580
No, he was very strict and frightening.

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:46.080
After my mother died,

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:48.710
I cried all the time, but he forced me
to practice swordsmanship.

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:56.020
I thought that my father never felt
pain, even when my mother died.

00:09:56.420 --> 00:10:03.890
However, I once saw him crying silently
while holding her kimono.

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:09.690
I thought, "Ah, an adult man can cry."

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:16.210
After that, I practiced with
the sword more seriously.

00:10:16.210 --> 00:10:17.840
I wanted to make my father happy.

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:22.380
I'm sure that your father is still happy.

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:04.220
What are you gaping at?

00:11:04.960 --> 00:11:06.120
A man like that...

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:07.430
What?

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:09.190
I wonder why he was able to kill people?

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:11.800
Don't ask questions like that of him, Kaoru.

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:16.530
I still wonder why I was a pickpocket
before I came here.

00:11:16.970 --> 00:11:22.340
But I can't erase something like that.
I can't forget about it either.

00:11:24.110 --> 00:11:25.840
Sorry. I am so sorry.

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:50.740
You've got nerve walking down the street

00:11:50.740 --> 00:11:53.260
in the middle of the day with a sword.

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:56.180
You're under arrest for violating
the law banning swords.

00:11:56.180 --> 00:11:57.110
Wait! Ujiki!

00:11:58.950 --> 00:12:00.780
Let me handle this. Sheathe your sword.

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:04.850
The Secretary of the Army?!

00:12:06.520 --> 00:12:07.750
Yes, sir!

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:10.120
Aritomo Yamagata?

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:13.190
I've been looking for you for ten years, Himura.

00:12:13.630 --> 00:12:14.820
He came to pick Kenshin up?

00:12:15.230 --> 00:12:18.700
Many colleagues are looking
forward to you coming back.

00:12:18.700 --> 00:12:20.360
Let's go back together.

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:25.440
Mr. Yamagata, I appreciate your
concern about me, however,

00:12:25.940 --> 00:12:28.170
I don't intend to take an honorable
position for murdering people.

00:12:36.850 --> 00:12:37.750
Himura!

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:40.710
Times have changed.

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:43.890
It's different from the last days of the
Tokugawa when your sword had power.

00:12:43.890 --> 00:12:48.000
In this Meiji era, a sword can't do anything at all.

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:53.530
With a sword, I can protect
people I can see.

00:13:06.980 --> 00:13:13.320
Kenshin, do you need a sword no
matter what? Can't you let it go?

00:13:15.660 --> 00:13:20.060
Back then, the sunset dyed the sky like this...

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:26.600
"Don't run away after you've
killed so many people."

00:13:30.440 --> 00:13:32.540
"Live with the sword and die with the sword."

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:36.530
"There is no other way for you to live."
Someone told me that.

00:13:37.480 --> 00:13:42.820
It's been ten years since then, but I
still don't understand what I can do.

00:13:43.720 --> 00:13:47.280
Until I find the answer, I can't put
down this reversed blade sword.

00:14:17.350 --> 00:14:20.120
Father, do you think I can do it?

00:14:20.120 --> 00:14:24.790
Share his pain and the weight of his sword?

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:30.860
Kenshin won't be back.

00:14:31.270 --> 00:14:32.230
What?

00:14:32.530 --> 00:14:35.370
So I was told to take care of this
house while he's gone.

00:14:35.370 --> 00:14:37.170
Why, Sanosuke?

00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:41.610
Jin'e has been targeting only patriots
of the Meiji Restoration.

00:14:41.610 --> 00:14:43.080
His next target is Kenshin.

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:46.510
So in order to avoid causing any trouble,

00:14:46.510 --> 00:14:48.510
he won't be back here for a while.

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:53.780
Look at me. Jin'e is not an ordinary enemy.

00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:55.920
Even if you go to help him, you
would only be a drag on him.

00:14:55.920 --> 00:14:57.020
Stay here quietly.

00:15:21.320 --> 00:15:22.210
Kenshi...

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:41.500
Has the Battosai gone dull?
To fall in love with a girl like this...

00:15:44.510 --> 00:15:48.880
Don't look at me like that.
I didn't kidnap you to eat.

00:15:48.880 --> 00:15:52.510
I know that. You did it because you
want to weaken him, you coward!

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:57.420
You don't understand. Now that I have
you as a hostage, he will go mad.

00:15:57.720 --> 00:16:00.750
The madness will make him revert to
how he used to be as an assassin.

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:04.430
I have no business with him as
he is now, having lost his spirit.

00:16:04.430 --> 00:16:06.120
Kenshin is still strong.

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:10.390
You don't know how strong he was
in the last days of the Tokugawa.

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:14.000
Just hearing stories about him,
people get goose pimples,

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:15.970
because of his cold and cruel sword.

00:16:16.470 --> 00:16:19.540
He is indeed the strongest assassin.

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:22.740
He is a man who has mastered how
to kill people with the sword.

00:16:25.780 --> 00:16:29.520
To fight him knowing it
might mean my death,

00:16:29.520 --> 00:16:31.610
it's the best murder to enjoy.

00:16:34.790 --> 00:16:38.160
Well, here comes the master of murder.

00:16:44.330 --> 00:16:45.260
You, girl!

00:17:34.850 --> 00:17:36.680
Remember, Battosai!

00:17:37.150 --> 00:17:38.620
Remember the smell of blood,

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:40.720
the feel of cutting flesh and bone,

00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:43.990
the fun and ecstasy of killing people.

00:17:51.570 --> 00:17:52.470
Come.

00:17:52.470 --> 00:17:54.400
The man who masters how to draw
the sword from the sheath...

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:57.830
That's the reason for his other name,
"Battosai," I've heard.

00:17:58.510 --> 00:18:01.610
Since he is a master of the Hiten Mitsurugi
style, with its godlike speed,

00:18:01.610 --> 00:18:04.140
he must be the fastest at drawing
his sword from the sheath.

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:09.110
However, I wonder how fast he can
draw now since his arm is injured?

00:18:12.620 --> 00:18:14.420
Now, time to fight!

00:18:29.600 --> 00:18:30.540
No!

00:18:36.980 --> 00:18:37.970
Miss Kaoru!

00:18:39.880 --> 00:18:42.350
Don't go back to being a murderer.

00:18:42.350 --> 00:18:47.320
You are no longer Battosai,
so please, don't...

00:18:47.320 --> 00:18:49.760
Well, let's finish up.

00:18:52.490 --> 00:18:54.930
What a nice feeling!

00:19:02.100 --> 00:19:04.200
The end of a murderer should be like this.

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:08.510
Well, my arm is now useless so it's
no fun for me to live without it.

00:19:09.380 --> 00:19:11.910
Don't look at me like that, Battosai.

00:19:11.910 --> 00:19:14.110
Your real character is a murderer, as I thought.

00:19:14.550 --> 00:19:20.150
A murderer is a murderer until he dies.
You can't be anything else...

00:19:41.440 --> 00:19:42.470
Kenshin...

00:19:44.440 --> 00:19:46.440
We need to stop the bleeding
as soon as possible.

00:19:49.280 --> 00:19:52.880
Kenshin, thank you for coming
here to rescue me.

00:19:53.390 --> 00:19:59.350
No, I'm the one to say thanks, not you.
I was almost...

00:19:59.790 --> 00:20:00.760
Don't say it.

00:20:01.560 --> 00:20:08.700
This is the record of this man's life;
one more scar on his small body.

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:11.830
A new scar... I am sorry.

00:20:22.380 --> 00:20:25.190
Cherry blossoms are beautiful
while they are out,

00:20:25.190 --> 00:20:26.850
but it's also beautiful when they are falling.

00:20:27.650 --> 00:20:31.280
Blossoms when they are falling...
Somehow I can't like them.

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:33.230
Sorry.

00:20:33.230 --> 00:20:34.990
Oh, no.

00:20:36.430 --> 00:20:39.960
You don't need to force yourself
to smile in front of me.

00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:45.340
I had a dream this morning.

00:20:46.970 --> 00:20:48.340
Of that time...

00:20:48.340 --> 00:20:49.470
During the last days of the Tokugawa?

00:20:50.840 --> 00:20:53.010
Blood was falling just like cherry blossoms.

00:20:53.610 --> 00:20:54.670
Kenshin...

00:20:55.880 --> 00:20:59.380
But a cherry tree is a cherry tree, not blood.

00:21:00.920 --> 00:21:03.960
Yes, matters of the past are
the same as dreams,

00:21:03.960 --> 00:21:07.720
and they'll fade in time
and disappear someday.

00:21:08.360 --> 00:21:09.730
I agree with you.

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:15.440
Someday, he will show me his smile
from the bottom of his heart.

00:21:15.870 --> 00:21:16.800
I believe so.

00:21:28.580 --> 00:21:29.680
Kenshin?!

00:21:48.840 --> 00:21:51.570
May 14 1878

00:21:54.710 --> 00:21:57.140
Extra! Extra! The Secretary of the
Interior has been assassinated!

00:21:57.140 --> 00:21:58.870
Secretary Ookubo was assassinated!

00:22:31.580 --> 00:22:41.580
I knew that the times needed him, and
I couldn't change his way of life.

00:22:50.330 --> 00:22:55.560
I know that. I knew that, but...

00:22:56.900 --> 00:22:59.030
Thank you so very much
for everything until now.

00:23:03.840 --> 00:23:05.970
Goodbye, Kaoru.

00:23:12.090 --> 00:23:14.820
I couldn't chase him then, either.

00:24:11.480 --> 00:24:14.570
On that night, the night when
Kenshin left for Kyoto,

00:24:15.080 --> 00:24:17.350
to hold Kenshin tight.

00:24:17.580 --> 00:24:18.550
What?

00:24:19.750 --> 00:24:21.050
Kenshin told me,

00:24:21.760 --> 00:24:25.780
"A crazy murderer is still living
deep inside of my heart."

00:24:26.230 --> 00:24:29.250
But, I accept him as he is.

00:24:29.930 --> 00:24:31.830
Don't tell me things like that.

00:24:32.870 --> 00:24:34.770
You need to tell that to him face to face.

00:24:35.040 --> 00:24:37.870
Idiot! I can't do that, so I'm telling you.

00:24:37.870 --> 00:24:41.430
What the hell is that? Think
about how I feel about it.

00:24:42.010 --> 00:24:44.310
Was that too stimulating for a kid like you?

00:24:44.680 --> 00:24:46.910
I can't believe women nowadays...

00:24:46.910 --> 00:24:47.880
Sorry.

00:24:48.780 --> 00:24:49.980
It's okay.

00:25:12.740 --> 00:25:14.070
Miss Kaoru?

00:25:15.040 --> 00:25:16.340
A guest for you?

00:25:16.880 --> 00:25:20.680
I will take care of her for now,
so hurry up and get some water.

00:25:31.460 --> 00:25:32.450
Kenshin!

00:25:33.660 --> 00:25:37.430
I chased you from Kyoto. Are you mad at me?

00:25:39.870 --> 00:25:40.800
Half.

00:25:44.910 --> 00:25:45.870
Half?

00:25:53.180 --> 00:25:57.210
My stupid student must be feeling that
he was burnt alive by the flame,

00:25:58.050 --> 00:26:03.890
the flame of the lives which he erased.

00:26:04.490 --> 00:26:07.290
And it will continue into the future...

00:26:07.930 --> 00:26:12.130
Even so, I want to be with him.

00:26:12.130 --> 00:26:16.760
If we can go home safely together
with him, forever...

00:26:17.400 --> 00:26:20.670
When the pottery is done, I will
give it to you. It's a tea cup.

00:26:21.410 --> 00:26:25.440
When you go back to Tokyo, use it to
serve good tea to my stupid student.

00:26:29.450 --> 00:26:30.420
Sure.

00:26:42.400 --> 00:26:43.390
Kenshin?

00:26:49.340 --> 00:26:52.740
I won't take my eyes off of you
and your battle, ever.

00:27:02.750 --> 00:27:04.240
I won't leave you, ever again.

00:27:21.530 --> 00:27:31.430
Someday, when you can
really rest... Until then...

00:27:59.040 --> 00:28:00.010
Ah, look!

00:28:04.010 --> 00:28:04.980
Father...

00:28:05.410 --> 00:28:08.280
Father, I was not able to bring you home.

00:28:09.350 --> 00:28:10.320
However...

00:28:11.690 --> 00:28:12.650
Kenshin.

00:28:16.820 --> 00:28:18.020
Welcome home.

00:28:26.700 --> 00:28:27.790
I'm home.

00:28:35.110 --> 00:28:36.340
His body is torn.

00:28:39.950 --> 00:28:43.470
His athletic skill is extremely outstanding.

00:28:44.120 --> 00:28:46.480
However, other than that, he's the
same as any ordinary person.

00:28:47.090 --> 00:28:49.920
If something happens next time,
it will be no surprise if he dies.

00:28:50.760 --> 00:28:51.750
Therefore,

00:28:52.130 --> 00:28:55.760
in order to make him feel strongly
about coming back to you alive,

00:28:55.760 --> 00:28:57.920
you have to be stronger.

00:28:58.770 --> 00:29:02.270
I wish I could, but I can't.
Only you can do so.

00:29:02.270 --> 00:29:06.400
The only person he said goodbye
to in Tokyo was you.

00:29:10.310 --> 00:29:12.400
Thank you, Miss Megumi.

00:29:18.490 --> 00:29:19.520
Hurry, hurry!

00:29:19.520 --> 00:29:20.780
Wait!

00:29:23.320 --> 00:29:24.520
From now on,

00:29:25.020 --> 00:29:28.320
the world will probably become

00:29:29.260 --> 00:29:32.630
calmer and more peaceful. No more war.

00:29:33.200 --> 00:29:38.370
And everybody can live
together forever. I hope so.

00:29:38.810 --> 00:29:40.310
That's impossible.

00:29:40.310 --> 00:29:41.270
What?

00:29:41.610 --> 00:29:45.750
Time goes by and swordsmanship is changing.

00:29:45.750 --> 00:29:48.680
There is no way that humans won't change.

00:29:49.620 --> 00:29:54.280
Someday everybody will part ways
and live their own life.

00:29:54.750 --> 00:29:56.780
It sounds lonely, but it's a fact.

00:29:57.090 --> 00:29:57.890
But I...

00:29:58.660 --> 00:30:02.460
I want to be with you forever, Kenshin.

00:30:03.930 --> 00:30:05.400
So please come back.

00:30:05.870 --> 00:30:07.200
Promise me.

00:30:07.670 --> 00:30:10.500
No matter what happens to you,
you'll come back to me alive.

00:30:19.050 --> 00:30:21.240
When I came back here from Kyoto,

00:30:22.120 --> 00:30:24.780
when I heard you saying "Welcome home,"

00:30:25.390 --> 00:30:27.290
I was really happy from the bottom of my heart.

00:30:28.320 --> 00:30:32.160
There is a person who welcomes a man like me.

00:30:33.390 --> 00:30:35.230
I have a place to come back to.

00:30:40.170 --> 00:30:43.400
This is the only place for me to come back to.

00:30:53.930 --> 00:30:58.170
Jinchu (Punishment by man)

00:30:58.990 --> 00:31:00.540
Jinchu...

00:31:05.460 --> 00:31:06.550
I have to go.

00:31:07.890 --> 00:31:08.830
Kenshin!

00:31:10.100 --> 00:31:11.260
Don't worry.

00:31:28.110 --> 00:31:28.980
Welcome h...

00:31:32.620 --> 00:31:34.350
Kenshin...

00:31:39.890 --> 00:31:41.630
You haven't eaten dinner yet, have you?

00:31:41.630 --> 00:31:44.460
I don't need it. I'm going to go to bed today.

00:32:14.060 --> 00:32:16.430
No! I can't ask him what happened.

00:32:17.500 --> 00:32:20.370
I've never seen him as pitiful as that.

00:32:20.570 --> 00:32:23.470
Jinchu

00:32:32.280 --> 00:32:33.250
Kenshin.

00:32:34.280 --> 00:32:38.240
Please eat something, even one bite, please.

00:32:42.490 --> 00:32:43.350
What is this?

00:32:44.390 --> 00:32:45.820
Mr. Hiko made it for me.

00:32:54.230 --> 00:32:57.400
I have something to talk to
you about, Miss Kaoru.

00:32:58.600 --> 00:33:03.300
The story about the grudge buried
in this cross-shaped scar

00:33:04.110 --> 00:33:06.840
and the meaning of "Jinchu"
which connects to the story.

00:33:31.000 --> 00:33:39.710
I murdered my wife, Tomoe Himura,
with my own hands.

00:33:52.090 --> 00:33:56.090
I thought he'd finally come back to me,

00:33:57.800 --> 00:34:01.960
but Kenshin's mind is still wandering
around somewhere.

00:34:25.160 --> 00:34:26.250
Kenshin...

00:35:07.700 --> 00:35:12.540
Your hand feels gentle

00:35:15.040 --> 00:35:19.570
You said so

00:35:22.380 --> 00:35:26.910
Tears come out

00:35:29.620 --> 00:35:34.060
Very quietly

00:35:37.100 --> 00:35:41.970
Seashore in spring

00:35:44.200 --> 00:35:49.070
Your head on my knees and fell asleep

00:35:51.640 --> 00:35:56.980
Your hair, gently

00:35:57.620 --> 00:36:04.460
When I combed with my fingers

00:36:07.330 --> 00:36:17.330
Suddenly, I felt like I understood everything

00:36:21.840 --> 00:36:31.840
All the pain in the heart goes home to the sky

00:36:39.430 --> 00:36:44.260
On your cheek

00:36:46.570 --> 00:36:51.600
The drops of the tears

00:36:53.810 --> 00:36:59.340
I told you it's spray from the sea

00:36:59.850 --> 00:37:06.080
I put my hands over your eyes to blind

00:37:12.290 --> 00:37:22.290
Please be here with me, I am here with you
